    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"During the months of August-October, 1998, the National Marine Fisheries Service and the New England scallop industry conducted a cooperative survey of Closed Area II to assess the sea scallop population after 3.5 years of closure to all fishing.  The area was closed in December 1994 to conserve fish stocks.  Most of the tows are concentrated in the southern part of Closed Area II (south of 41o 30'N) and in the northernmost part (north of 41o 50'N).  The central area between 41o 30' and 41o 50'N was sparsely sampled.  See the location map for the 1998 survey.\r\n\r\nThe survey was conducted with commercial scallop vessels, each towing two 15-foot wide dredges at a speed of 4.5 kts for 10 minutes.  Each tow covered a distance of approximately 0.75 nm or 1400 meters.  In all, data were collected from 1581 stations.  See the ca21998srvorigB.txt file for a tabulation of the original data.  A new lefthand column of consecutive station numbers has been added to facilitate use of the data.\r\n\r\nThe data include statistics on the scallop (and scallop meat) catch and on the bycatch of lobster, skates (all species combined), and 9 groundfish species (American Plaice, Atlantic Cod, Goosefish, Haddock, Summer Flounder, Windowpane Flounder, Winter Flounder, Witch Flounder, and Yellowtail Flounder).\r\n\r\nThe survey results were used here to plot species distribution maps.  For the species abundance maps, the data includes all tows of 9, 10 and 11 minutes duration (895 tows; ca21998srvabundA.pdf and ca21998srvabundB.txt) and excludes all replicate tows at sites where repeated tows were conducted in depletion experiments.  For the species presence/absence maps, the data includes all tows (1544; ca21998srvpresabA.pdf and ca21998srvpresabB.txt ) except for those with bad navigation.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
